</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Training Set Size</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.T5" title="In Appendix B Prompt ‣ Distribution Shift Alignment Helps LLMs Simulate Survey Response Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> presents the training set sizes for the different datasets used in <a href="#S2.T1" title="In 2.4 Fine-Tuning Method ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Distribution Shift Alignment Helps LLMs Simulate Survey Response Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The reduced size of the training sets for CGSS and CFPS is due to the relatively smaller volumes of data available in these datasets compared to the others.</p>
</div>
</section>
